## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/models/gemini_model_example.py - Example script showing how to create a ChatAgent using Gemini models with tools (TerminalToolkit used in example, can replace with SearchToolkit for duckduckgo)
- examples/toolkits/role_playing_with_functions.py - Example showing usage of SearchToolkit with duckduckgo search tool in a role-playing multi-agent setup

## Implementation
- camel/models/gemini_model.py - Implementation of GeminiModel class, the LLM provider integration for Gemini models
- camel/toolkits/search_toolkit.py - Implementation of SearchToolkit including the duckduckgo search method and get_tools() method returning duckduckgo tool
- camel/configs/gemini_config.py - Configuration class GeminiConfig for Gemini model parameters

## Tests
- test/models/test_gemini_model.py - Test cases for GeminiModel including message processing and tool call merging

These files provide the necessary model, config, and toolkit implementations plus usage examples to create an agent using Gemini model with duckduckgo search tool to answer questions. The example in examples/models/gemini_model_example.py can be adapted to use SearchToolkit().get_tools() or specifically SearchToolkit().search_duckduckgo as the tools list. The role_playing_with_functions.py example shows how to use SearchToolkit's duckduckgo search tool in an agent context. The test file ensures GeminiModel behavior is correct.
